@page "/docs/get-started/ai-assistants"

@* Connecting an AI assistant to IzzyBlazor's docs: the MCP server at /mcp (Services/Mcp), llms.txt
   and the API metadata. The client settings were the documented ones for each client in Oct 2026. *@

<ArticlePage Section="get-started" Slug="ai-assistants">
    <Lead>
        Assistants guess at a library they haven't seen, and IzzyBlazor is newer than their training. Connect yours to
        IzzyBlazor's MCP server and it looks up components, parameters and working examples for the release on this site
        instead.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">The server</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            The server is at <Code>@Endpoint</Code>. It uses the Streamable HTTP transport and needs no sign-in or key. Its
            tools only read the docs, and it answers for the release this site documents.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Claude Code</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="bash">claude mcp add --transport http izzyblazor @Endpoint</Code>
        <TextBlock>Add <Code>--scope project</Code> to save it in the repository's <Code>.mcp.json</Code> for everyone on the project.</TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">VS Code and Visual Studio</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Add the server to <Code>.vscode/mcp.json</Code> in VS Code, or <Code>.mcp.json</Code> next to the solution in
            Visual Studio, then use it from Copilot's agent mode:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="json" Title=".vscode/mcp.json">@VsCodeJson</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Cursor</Heading>
        <Code Block Language="json" Title=".cursor/mcp.json">@CursorJson</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Claude apps</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            In Claude's desktop app or on claude.ai, open Settings, then Connectors, add a custom connector and paste
            <Code>@Endpoint</Code>. Any other client that supports Streamable HTTP takes the same address.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Tools</Heading>
        <Table Items="Tools" Caption="Tools" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <TemplateColumn Title="Tool" Width="Length.Rem(10)"><code>@context!.Name</code></TemplateColumn>
            <TemplateColumn Title="Answers with">@context!.Answers</TemplateColumn>
        </Table>
        <TextBlock>
            Answers are Markdown with links to this site. Ask for what you're building ("a settings form that posts on a
            static page") and the assistant picks the tools; naming IzzyBlazor in the request helps it reach for them.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Without MCP</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                <Anchor Href="llms.txt">llms.txt</Anchor>: what IzzyBlazor is and a link to every article and component, for
                assistants that read a site.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <Anchor Href="izzyblazor.api.json">API metadata</Anchor>: every component's parameters, events, methods and
                types as one JSON file, for your own tools.
            </ListItem>
        </List>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/get-started/blazor-web-app">Blazor Web App</Anchor>: install the package and set up a new app.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">Render modes</Anchor>: what components do on static and interactive pages.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Endpoint = "https://izzyblazor.com/mcp";

    private sealed record Tool(string Name, string Answers);

    private static readonly Tool[] Tools =
    [
        new("search", "Components, parameters, types, examples and articles that match some words"),
        new("list_components", "Every component by category, with a summary and any mode limits"),
        new("get_component", "A component's API: parameters with types and defaults, events, methods, mode support, parts, example ids and accessibility"),
        new("get_type", "An enum's values, a type's members, or the shared style props"),
        new("get_example", "An example's whole .razor source"),
        new("get_article", "An article or a component's Overview, with its examples' source"),
    ];

    private const string VsCodeJson = """
        {
          "servers": {
            "izzyblazor": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://izzyblazor.com/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;

    private const string CursorJson = """
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "izzyblazor": {
              "url": "https://izzyblazor.com/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;
}
